<BaseLayout title="Build & test" description="How SIGRUN compiles and boots: the nightly toolchain, static-relocation rustflags, the linker script, ISO creation with GRUB, QEMU runs, and the test strategy.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Tooling · build &amp; test</p>
  <h1>Build &amp; test: from cargo to a booting ISO</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Building an OS means telling the toolchain exactly what you are not getting: no std, no libc, no dynamic
    linking, no OS. SIGRUN's build encodes those assumptions in <code class="mono">.cargo/config.toml</code>,
    a linker script, and a set of scripts.
  </p>

